.\" Origin: EmberBSD Realtek Bluetooth patch loader, AI-assisted.
.Dd November 9, 2026
.Dt RTLBTFW 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rtlbtfw
.Nd load patch firmware into a Realtek Bluetooth controller
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl nv
.Op Fl c Ar config
.Op Fl f Ar firmware
.Ar device
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Realtek Bluetooth controllers such as the RTL8821CE start with ROM firmware.
The RTL8821CE ROM reports HCI version 4.2 and the local name
.Dq RTK_BT_4.1 .
The vendor publishes a patch for the ROM through linux-firmware.
The controller keeps the patch until its next power cycle.
.Nm
sends the patch to the controller with vendor HCI commands through the
raw HCI socket of
.Ar device ,
for example
.Li ubt0 .
.Pp
.Nm
reads the local version of the controller.
It stops with success when the controller is not a Realtek device or
when the version is not a known ROM identity.
Patched firmware reports its own version, so a second run makes no change.
Otherwise it reads the ROM version, selects the matching patch from the
firmware file, appends the config file, and downloads the image in
fragments of 252 bytes.
After the download it reads the version again and resets the controller
in the same way as
.Ql btconfig reset ,
so the Bluetooth stack reads the patched features.
.Pp
The firmware files come from the
.Pa rtl_bt
directory of linux-firmware.
.Nm
searches each directory of the
.Li hw.firmware.path
sysctl for
.Pa rtl_bt/ Ns Ao chip Ac Ns Pa _fw.bin
and
.Pa rtl_bt/ Ns Ao chip Ac Ns Pa _config.bin .
The RTL8852C firmware file ends in
.Pa _fw_v2.bin .
The config file is optional, except for the RTL8723D and RTL8822B.
The RTL8821C uses
.Pa rtl8821c_fw.bin
and
.Pa rtl8821c_config.bin .
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Fl c Ar config
Read the config file from
.Ar config
instead of the firmware search path.
.It Fl f Ar firmware
Read the firmware file from
.Ar firmware
instead of the firmware search path.
.It Fl n
Select the patch and print the image size, but do not download it.
.It Fl v
Print the controller version and the selected patch.
.El
.Pp
If
.Ar device
is not enabled,
.Nm
enables it first, because HCI commands reach only an enabled unit.
The device stays enabled afterwards, also with
.Fl n
and for controllers that need no patch.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Pa -compact
.It Pa rtl_bt/
Firmware directory below each entry of the
.Va hw.firmware.path
sysctl.
The
.Li sysutils/rtl-bt-firmware
package installs
.Pa /usr/pkg/libdata/firmware/rtl_bt/ .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Nm
exits 0 without a download when the controller is not a Realtek device
or already runs patch firmware.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Load the patch into the RTL8821CE and show the result:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# rtlbtfw -v ubt0
ubt0: hci 8.000c lmp 8 manufacturer 0x005d subversion 0x8821
ubt0: rtl8821c rom version 1
ubt0: image 34926 bytes, 139 fragments
ubt0: rtl8821c patch loaded, hci revision 0x000c -> 0x75b8, lmp subversion 0xf098
.Ed
.Pp
The patched controller reports the firmware version 0x75b8f098 in its
HCI revision and LMP subversion fields.
.Pp
The
.Xr rc.conf 5
variable
.Va bluetooth_firmware
makes
.Pa /etc/rc.d/bluetooth
run
.Nm
for each controller before it configures them.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ubt 4 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
.Xr btconfig 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in EmberBSD.
The download protocol follows the
.Fx
utility of the same name by Adrian Chadd and Vladimir Kondratyev.
EmberBSD reimplements it over the
.Nx
HCI socket.
.Sh BUGS
Only the
.Dq Realtech
.Pq sic
firmware format is supported.
The raw image of the RTL8723A is rejected.
Files in the
.Dq RTBTCore
format of newer chips are rejected.
Only the RTL8821CE was tested on hardware.
.Pp
.Pa /etc/rc.d/bluetooth
runs
.Nm
at boot.
A controller attached later needs a manual run.
